From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:04:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/m720q_m920q: No FSP-M HECI retries with the ME
 disabled

With the ME disabled in the setup ("me_state", soft temporary disable),
FspMemoryInit took 15.24 s on some boots, constant to the millisecond,
with a valid training cache ("does not need update"), and 0.23 s on
others with the same build and cache: FSP-M sends the ME its HECI
messages (ChipsetInitMessage, SendDidMsg and the rest are on in its
defaults) and, when they get no answer, retries them with its timeouts.
A test build with DisableHeciRetry set gave 0.23 s.

Set FspmTestConfig.DisableHeciRetry when the setup asks for the ME
disabled, or when HFSTS1 already shows the soft temporary disable; an
ME that runs keeps the retries, which can help it answer late. HFSTS1
alone is not enough: before FSP-M it did not show the disable on the
boots measured, although ramstage logged it, so romstage also logs it.
The same pattern as Dasharo's dasharo-issues #1874, where a default of
the FSP waited on a bus that never answered.

TEST=On the M920x with the ME disabled: ci-155 and ci-157 (the HFSTS1
check alone, which never matched) gave 15.24 s on some warm reboots and
0.23 s on others; ci-156 (DisableHeciRetry from the devicetree) 0.23 s.
Still to test with this patch: "ME: HFSTS1 before FSP-M" and "ME
disabled: no HECI retries in FSP-M" in the log at every boot and
FspMemoryInit about 0.2 s on several reboots; with the ME enabled, no
such line and a normal boot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c
index d0ea9454c5..9aef1f911b 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 #include <device/pci_def.h>
 #include <device/pci_ops.h>
 #include <fsp/api.h>
+#include <intelblocks/cse.h>
 #include <mainboard/ec.h>
 #include <option.h>
 #include <soc/cnl_memcfg_init.h>
@@ -126,4 +127,18 @@ void mainboard_memory_init_params(FSPM_UPD *memupd)
 		memupd->FspmConfig.PcieRpEnableMask &= ~(1 << 5);
 
 	memupd->FspmConfig.Peg0Enable = peg_enable(memupd);
+
+	/*
+	 * With the ME disabled (Security > Management Engine), FSP-M's HECI
+	 * messages get no answer, and on some boots its retries cost 15.2 s in
+	 * FspMemoryInit, a valid training cache or not; without them it takes
+	 * 0.23 s. Before FSP-M, HFSTS1 does not always show the soft temporary
+	 * disable yet, so the setup option decides; an ME that runs keeps them.
+	 */
+	const uint32_t hfsts1 = me_read_config32(PCI_ME_HFSTS1);
+	printk(BIOS_INFO, "ME: HFSTS1 before FSP-M: %08x\n", hfsts1);
+	if (!cse_is_me_state_requested_enabled() || cse_is_hfs1_com_soft_temp_disable()) {
+		memupd->FspmTestConfig.DisableHeciRetry = 1;
+		printk(BIOS_INFO, "ME disabled: no HECI retries in FSP-M\n");
+	}
 }
